|term[description] :status settled :defined-by def-descriptors :anchor descriptor-kinds
  :word description
  :avoid [query filter]
  A predicate the world satisfies — nothing was ever bound; the connection is recomputed from whatever satisfies it at each use.
  |invariants
    - Is a kind of [[term/descriptor]]
    - Is the dual of [[term/designator]]
    - Picks out zero or more [[term/referent]] — plurality is a feature
    - Is never the act's conjunction: an act HAS one or more descriptors; a description IS one kind of descriptor
  |note :audience maintainer
    Steward skepticism stands (def-descriptors WN): "silent re-satisfaction" as this kind's failure mode may dissolve under an event-sourced foundation; Temporal chapter adjudicates.
